From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:38:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0098: words of large resource tables are read ahead
 while memory holds their settled value

0063 let a word of a table of resources be read without waiting for the GPU once it came out of eight
waits unchanged, but only in a range of at most 256 bytes the GPU writes: counters. Clair Obscur waits
four times an image for words of its tables; two of them are always 0, in ranges of 1.9 and 2.4 MB a pass
rewrites every frame: 3.6 ms of the command thread an image, and each wait drains the GPU. 0078 (not
delivered) let any range speculate and was wrong five times, each a draw recorded with a wrong resource.
The trace of 0095 shows why: Clair Obscur alternates that word with another one, a frame in four, and
when it comes back to it the region holds 0xffffffff, which the GPU then clears to 0. The value in memory
was not the one the GPU had left there: the region served something else meanwhile.

- Any range earns trust, as counters do: eight waits that leave the word unchanged, twice as many after
  each difference.
- A trusted word is read ahead only while memory holds the value it settled at: the value after its last
  wait, or after the check of its last read ahead. Otherwise it waits, and keeps its trust.
- A word last seen in a range larger than a counter is revoked for good at its first difference: a table
  entry that moves. Counters keep their five.
- The perf log counts the words read ahead, held (trusted, memory elsewhere: they waited) and missed.

What a miss costs, as before: the draw that read ahead was recorded with the word in memory; the check
after the GPU's work withdraws the trust, says so on the console, and the word waits from then on.

The recompiler and the pipeline code are left alone: the shader store keeps its stamp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/common/commandThreadProfile.h             |  9 +++-
 .../host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp   | 50 +++++++++++++------
 .../host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.h     |  9 ++--
 3 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/common/commandThreadProfile.h b/src/common/commandThreadProfile.h
index 5f461b42..4b26426e 100644
--- a/src/common/commandThreadProfile.h
+++ b/src/common/commandThreadProfile.h
@@ -76,6 +76,12 @@ enum class Event : uint8_t {
 	GpuWaits,       // Waits of this thread for the GPU.
 	MemoryAllocations, // Vulkan device memory allocated (driver buffer objects), any thread.
 	MemoryReleases,
+	// GameFlex (0098): the words of resource tables in ranges the GPU may still write. Read ahead: trusted and
+	// taken from memory without waiting; held: trusted, but memory did not hold the value the GPU left there last,
+	// so they waited; missed: read ahead, and the GPU wrote another value afterwards.
+	SrtReadAhead,
+	SrtHeld,
+	SrtMissed,
 	Count
 };
 
@@ -798,7 +804,8 @@ struct Report {
 [[nodiscard]] constexpr const char* Name(Event event) noexcept {
 	constexpr const char* NAMES[EVENT_COUNT] = {
 	    "packets", "draws",       "dispatches", "barriers",    "command buffers", "submits",
-	    "retries", "label polls", "label waits GPU", "label waits CPU", "trusted waits", "GPU waits", "allocations", "releases"};
+	    "retries", "label polls", "label waits GPU", "label waits CPU", "trusted waits", "GPU waits", "allocations", "releases",
+	    "SRT words read ahead", "SRT words held", "SRT words missed"};
 	return NAMES[static_cast<size_t>(event)];
 }
 
diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp
index e42dfe91..6992f4bc 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.cpp
@@ -1119,10 +1119,19 @@ bool BufferCache::HasPendingGpuWrites(uint64_t vaddr, uint64_t size) {
 // (Astro Bot's light counter: 4 then 6 for good) earned it back nowhere and cost two full drains an image,
 // 33 ms, once the thread stopped waiting for labels (0072): the trust comes back after twice as many unchanged
 // waits as the time before, and only the fifth difference revokes the word for good.
+//
+// GameFlex (0098): words of large ranges too. Clair Obscur waits four times an image for words of its tables, two of
+// them always 0 in ranges of 1.9 and 2.4 MB a pass rewrites every frame: 3.6 ms of the command thread and two drains
+// of the GPU an image. 0078 let any range speculate and was wrong five times, each a draw recorded with a wrong
+// resource: a word Clair Obscur alternates with another, a frame in four, held 0xffffffff in memory when the game came
+// back to it, which the GPU then cleared to 0. The value in memory was not the one the GPU had left there: the
+// region served something else meanwhile. A trusted word is now read ahead only while memory holds the value it
+// settled at, after its last wait or check; otherwise it waits, and keeps its trust. A word of a range larger than a
+// counter that is still wrong is a table entry that moves: its first difference revokes it for good.
 namespace {
 constexpr uint32_t kSpeculationConfirmations = 8;
-constexpr uint32_t kSpeculationMisses        = 5; // differences before the word is revoked for good
-constexpr uint64_t kSpeculationRangeBytes    = 256; // a counter, not a table the GPU fills
+constexpr uint32_t kSpeculationMisses        = 5;   // differences before the word is revoked for good
+constexpr uint64_t kCounterRangeBytes        = 256; // a counter, not a table the GPU fills
 } // namespace
 
 void BufferCache::VerifySrtSpeculations() {
@@ -1137,18 +1146,22 @@ void BufferCache::VerifySrtSpeculations() {
 		}
 		speculation.verify_tick = 0;
 		uint32_t landed = 0;
-		if (!LibKernel::Memory::TryReadBacking(address, &landed, sizeof(landed)) ||
-		    landed == speculation.used) {
+		if (!LibKernel::Memory::TryReadBacking(address, &landed, sizeof(landed))) {
 			return true;
 		}
+		speculation.settled = landed;
+		if (landed == speculation.used) {
+			return true;
+		}
+		Common::CommandThreadProfile::Count(Common::CommandThreadProfile::Event::SrtMissed);
 		speculation.trusted       = false;
 		speculation.confirmations = 0;
-		speculation.revoked       = ++speculation.misses >= kSpeculationMisses;
+		speculation.revoked       = ++speculation.misses >= (speculation.large ? 1u : kSpeculationMisses);
 		static uint32_t misses = 0;
 		if (misses++ < 50) {
-			std::printf("SRT speculation: the GPU wrote 0x%08x at 0x%016" PRIx64 " after 0x%08x was used; "
+			std::printf("SRT speculation: the GPU wrote 0x%08x at 0x%016" PRIx64 " after 0x%08x was used%s; "
 			            "this word waits again%s\n",
-			            landed, address, speculation.used,
+			            landed, address, speculation.used, speculation.large ? " (large range)" : "",
 			            speculation.revoked ? " from now on" : " until it holds still for longer");
 		}
 		return true;
@@ -1176,12 +1189,17 @@ bool BufferCache::FinishPendingGpuWritesUnder(std::span<const uint64_t> addresse
 		if (speculation.trusted) {
 			uint32_t used = 0;
 			if (LibKernel::Memory::TryReadBacking(address, &used, sizeof(used))) {
-				if (speculation.verify_tick == 0) {
-					speculation.used = used;
-					m_srt_verifications.push_back(address);
+				// Memory holds what the GPU left there last (or what an unchecked read ahead took): read ahead.
+				if (used == (speculation.verify_tick != 0 ? speculation.used : speculation.settled)) {
+					if (speculation.verify_tick == 0) {
+						speculation.used = used;
+						m_srt_verifications.push_back(address);
+					}
+					speculation.verify_tick = std::max(speculation.verify_tick, range->tick);
+					Common::CommandThreadProfile::Count(Common::CommandThreadProfile::Event::SrtReadAhead);
+					continue;
 				}
-				speculation.verify_tick = std::max(speculation.verify_tick, range->tick);
-				continue;
+				Common::CommandThreadProfile::Count(Common::CommandThreadProfile::Event::SrtHeld);
 			}
 		}
 		uint32_t before = 0;
@@ -1203,9 +1221,11 @@ bool BufferCache::FinishPendingGpuWritesUnder(std::span<const uint64_t> addresse
 		m_scheduler.Finish();
 		Common::CommandThreadProfile::EndWordWait(ctp_wait);
 		m_pending_gpu_writes.Clear();
-		if (!speculation.revoked && range_size <= kSpeculationRangeBytes) {
-			uint32_t after = 0;
-			LibKernel::Memory::TryReadBacking(address, &after, sizeof(after));
+		uint32_t after = 0;
+		LibKernel::Memory::TryReadBacking(address, &after, sizeof(after));
+		speculation.settled = after;
+		speculation.large   = range_size > kCounterRangeBytes;
+		if (!speculation.revoked) {
 			if (after != before) {
 				speculation.confirmations = 0;
 			} else if (++speculation.confirmations >= kSpeculationConfirmations << speculation.misses) {
diff --git a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.h b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.h
index abf74515..e25d3de6 100644
--- a/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.h
+++ b/src/graphics/host_gpu/renderer/cache/bufferCache.h
@@ -101,14 +101,17 @@ public:
 	// As FinishPendingGpuWrites, for the 4-byte reads of the SRT walker; true when it waited.
 	bool FinishPendingGpuWritesUnder(std::span<const uint64_t> addresses);
 	// A word of a table of resources inside a range the GPU may still write, read without waiting once its value
-	// came out of eight waits unchanged; the GPU's value is compared afterwards. A difference withdraws the trust,
-	// which comes back after twice as many unchanged waits each time; the fifth revokes the word for good.
+	// came out of eight waits unchanged, and only while memory holds the value the GPU left there last; the GPU's
+	// value is compared afterwards. A difference withdraws the trust, which comes back after twice as many unchanged
+	// waits each time; the fifth revokes the word for good, the first one in a range larger than a counter.
 	struct SrtSpeculation {
 		uint32_t confirmations = 0; // consecutive waits that changed nothing
 		bool     trusted       = false;
-		bool     revoked       = false; // wrong five times: never trusted again
+		bool     revoked       = false; // wrong five times (once in a large range): never trusted again
+		bool     large         = false; // last seen in a range larger than a counter (kCounterRangeBytes)
 		uint32_t misses        = 0;     // differences seen so far
 		uint32_t used          = 0;     // the value read without waiting
+		uint32_t settled       = 0;     // the value after the last wait or check: what the GPU left there last
 		uint64_t verify_tick   = 0;     // the GPU work it skipped waiting for; 0 when nothing is to verify
 	};
 	void VerifySrtSpeculations();
